&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2566&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2566&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2903&quot; title=&quot;Make setting of working directory to user-home optional for shell interpreter&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-2903&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-2903&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; Make setting of working directory to user-home optional for shell interpreter&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;
	&lt;ol&gt;
		&lt;li&gt;
		&lt;ol&gt;
			&lt;li&gt;What is this PR for?&lt;br/&gt;
    With &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2841&quot; title=&quot;shell interpreter complained that working directory &amp;#39;.&amp;#39; can not be found in docker enviroment&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-2841&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-2841&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt;, it had changed the default working directory of Shell Interpreter from the relative path where Zeppelin is running to user-home. This is to make the configuration optional.&lt;/li&gt;
		&lt;/ol&gt;
		&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;/ol&gt;
	&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;



&lt;ol&gt;
