                            <comment id="16153385" author="sanjay.dasgupta@gmail.com" created="Tue, 5 Sep 2017 09:41:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Allow me to suggest that this may not be necessary.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Since the purpose of the shell interpreter is to run a shell script (the lines of the command provided to it), the interpreter&apos;s behavior should be as close to that of a real shell as possible.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So if the author of a script desires to run it in the home directory, the simple addition of a &quot;cd&quot; command at the top of the script should achieve that result. This would be completely transparent and natural to those reading the script later.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The need to correct the problem caused by Docker-hosting is IMHO a separate issue, and should not be mixed with configuration mechanisms.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Submitted for your consideration.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16153407" author="prabhjyotsingh" created="Tue, 5 Sep 2017 09:57:15 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=sanjay.dasgupta%40gmail.com&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;sanjay.dasgupta@gmail.com&quot;&gt;sanjay.dasgupta@gmail.com&lt;/a&gt; I believe this is what used to happen before &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-2841&quot; title=&quot;shell interpreter complained that working directory &amp;#39;.&amp;#39; can not be found in docker enviroment&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;ZEPPELIN-2841&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;ZEPPELIN-2841&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; and this is how shell interpreter will behave after this &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/pull/2566&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;PR-2566&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;image-wrap&quot; style=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;img src=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/attachment/12885343/Screen%20Shot%202017-09-05%20at%203.17.48%20PM.png&quot; width=&quot;100%&quot; style=&quot;border: 0px solid black&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Now to detect if Zeppelin is running in any Docker-hosting or any other encapsulated environment would be bit trivial and hence, I&apos;m in this PR, with the help to this variable `shell.working.directory.user.home` which either starts this interpreter in the user-home directory (if set to true) or starts in the relative directory where Zeppelin-server is running (which is by default).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Let me know what you think of it.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
